{"seq":17,"trial_id":"harness-zero-select-2026-11/zero-full-a-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-05T20:47:23.896Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"a008cebaaff2e1d081ea91e08afb193aaf714f10dd8f73d67c2ab82f76dffbf8","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes:\n\n- **#PD-4492**, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers at the Eau Claire yard (Dock Doors 14–18, 04:00 shift) weren't getting their SMS bay assignments when they checked in at the gatehouse kiosk. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct shift got through fine. The note also has a follow-up to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n- **#4419**, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners couldn't read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. The note says it went to tier-2 support for firmware testing. It has no date, so I can't tell how current that is.\n\nThe numbers look alike (4492 and 4419), so watch for typos when you copy them over.\n\nTwo other Moss notes mention Quarrendon but give no ticket number: the 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in. #4409 and #4412 in the Central handoffs note belong to a Central account, not Quarrendon. Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" (one R) is about a different company that isn't a customer.\n\nI only looked at Moss's shared notes, not the account's ticket system, so there may be other Quarrendon tickets Moss never wrote down."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
